        "text": "Established on the `cas-certificate` route. Franel is the standard demonstration that a definite hypergeometric sum can be P-recursive without being hypergeometric: there is a recurrence, there is no closed form, and this fact claims exactly the former. `cas.symbolic-gamma-arguments-avoid-poles` is NOT in the footprint because no symbolic base case is involved -- the recurrence alone is the statement.",
